# 107 - §6 (.40): there is no truthiness anywhere. A non-Bool if-condition is
# a Type error at the condition's line (3, the Var node - §6 .46 says the
# innermost failing node, never the enclosing statement), and the line printed
# before it is KEPT (§3: a program that fails at line 9 has the output of
# lines 1..8 and then the error).
#
# Wording is Value::as_bool in the frozen value.rs on master. See bead
# bd_30-agents-2jk.55: bead .39 proposes "condition must be Bool, found Int"
# for this case and the two disagree; this file follows the merged frozen file.
--- source
let n = 1;
print "first";
if n {
  print "never";
}
--- expect
first
error: Type at line 3: expected Bool, got Int
